WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.232
In the last years of Western Han, the court was in chaos and the people's lives were hard.

00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:08.856
Wang Mang seized the throne and founded the Xin dynasty.

00:00:09.156 --> 00:00:12.588
People everywhere rose up in revolt.

00:00:12.588 --> 00:00:17.076
The young Liu Xiu also led an army, gradually gaining the advantage.

00:00:17.376 --> 00:00:22.608
His army was strictly disciplined and high in morale, its banners flying.

00:00:22.608 --> 00:00:27.096
After years of campaigning, Liu Xiu reunified most of the land.

00:00:27.396 --> 00:00:32.388
In the year 25, Liu Xiu formally ascended the throne as emperor — known to history as Emperor Guangwu.

00:00:32.688 --> 00:00:38.328
He put the officials in order, let the farmers return to their fields, and the land gradually regained order.

00:00:38.628 --> 00:00:43.956
The Eastern Han was founded, and the people lived in peace and contentment, celebrating the calm.

00:00:43.956 --> 00:00:49.788
Later generations called this restoration of Han rule the 'Guangwu Restoration.'

